==English==

===Alternative forms===
* [[menage]]

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|xno|en}} {{term|meinage|lang=fro}}, {{term|maynage}}, {{etyl|fro|en}} {{term|mainage|lang=fro}}, {{term|menage}}, from {{term|mainer||to stay}}; with later influence after {{etyl|fr|en}} {{term|ménage|lang=fr}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/mɛˈnɑːʒ/|/meɪˈnɑːʒ/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[household]]; a [[domestic]] situation. {{defdate|from 14th c.}}
#* '''1939''', {{w|Raymond Chandler}}, ''The Big Sleep'', Penguin 2011, p. 39:
#*: It smelled of ether and something else, possibly laudanum. I had never tried the mixture but it seemed to go pretty well with the Geiger '''''ménage'''''.
# {{context|now|_|Scotland}} A type of [[cooperative]] society whereby all members pay a regular sum of [[savings]], or through which goods can be paid for in [[installment]]s. {{defdate|from 19th c.}}
# A group of people living together in a [[sexual]] relationship. {{defdate|from 20th c.}}

